Opening this just for discussion, this change is not approved by any other maintainer.

Replace the `index.js` entry point (`simple-icons`) with the current icons entry point (`simple-icons/icons`). My reasoning for this is that the majority of users will import the icon objects from `simple-icons/icons` and not import the `simpleIcons` object with all the icon data in `simple-icons`. It is already possible to perform a computation on each icon like so:
```js
import * as icons from 'simple-icons/icons'

for (const icon in icons) {
    // do stuff
}
```
The only use case that this removes support for is using `simpleIcons.Get`. I think users should solve this on their end, which is easily possible with a loop over each icon.

